stream
BT /F1 11 Tf 14 TL 50 740 Td
(Friday: Project Notes) '
() '
(Friday is a voice-first personal assistant built by Aditya in Bengaluru. It runs on) '
(his own laptop and is controlled by holding the Right Ctrl key while speaking, which) '
(is called push-to-talk.) '
() '
(For speech to text, Friday uses faster-whisper with the base.en model. For text to) '
(speech, it uses Piper with the en_US-amy-medium voice. Piper speaks the reply one) '
(sentence at a time.) '
() '
(The main language model is Groq running gpt-oss-20b. If Groq fails, Friday falls back) '
(to Gemini. Both are called through one file named llm.py.) '
() '
(Friday uses LangGraph to run each command. The graph goes from the router to a safety) '
(check, then to either a skill or the language model, and finally to the reply.) '
() '
(All data is stored in SQLite. This includes chat history, reminders, lists, traces) '
(and documents.) '
() '
(Reminders are scheduled with APScheduler and saved in SQLite, so they survive a) '
(restart. Friday cannot yet repeat reminders, list them or cancel them.) '
() '
(The music skill uses the Spotify Web API. It plays only on the device named ADI7 and) '
(never falls back to another device. Friday cannot yet play playlists or albums by) '
(name, and it cannot set the volume by spoken numbers like volume fifty.) '
() '
(The chat skill remembers the last six turns of conversation. A turn is one message) '
(from the user plus Friday's reply.) '
() '
(Math is handled by a safe parser that never uses eval. Lists and notes are stored in) '
(a table called list_items.) '
() '
(The catch skill is always registered last. If a command sounds like a list, reminder) '
(or timer command but is garbled, it asks the user to say it again instead of letting) '
(the language model pretend it saved something.) '
() '
(Secrets such as API keys live only in the .env file and the .secrets folder, and both) '
(are ignored by git.) '
() '
ET
endstream
